@startuml MagicLinkSSO-Browser-SSO-Flow

title Magic Link SSO Shared Browser Sign-In (Hosted UI)
hide footbox

participant "User's browser" as Browser
participant "Application A\n(SDK or Gate)" as AppA
participant "SSO server" as SSO
participant "Email inbox" as Email
participant "Application B\n(SDK or Gate)" as AppB

== Enter Application A Without a Valid Local Session ==

Browser -> AppA: Open protected URL / sign-in start
AppA -> SSO: GET /sso/capabilities (backend)
SSO --> AppA: Supported browser SSO capabilities
AppA -> AppA: Create state + PKCE S256 transaction;\nretain full returnUrl in encrypted cookie
AppA --> Browser: Set transaction cookie; redirect to issuer
Browser -> SSO: GET /sso/authorize\nredirectUri, state, codeChallenge, scope
SSO -> SSO: Validate exact registration;\nread host-only central session cookie

alt Existing identity lacks access and prompt is not login
    SSO --> Browser: Access denied + explicit account change\n(no automatic email)
else Existing identity allowed, or fresh verification needed
    opt No valid central session, or prompt=login
        Browser -> SSO: Submit email to POST /sso/signin
        SSO -> SSO: Check current site/scope grant
        SSO -> Email: Send one-time magic link + optional OTP
        alt Magic link
            Email --> Browser: Open GET /sso/verify (preview only)
            Browser -> SSO: Confirm identity; POST /sso/verify (CSRF)
        else Email OTP
            Browser -> SSO: Enter code; POST /sso/otp (CSRF)
        end
        SSO -> SSO: Consume email grant once;\ncreate central identity session
        SSO --> Browser: Set issuer-only HttpOnly session cookie
    end
    opt Identity verified and current target grant allowed
        SSO -> SSO: Issue one-time code bound to\ncentral session, callback, scope and PKCE
        SSO --> Browser: Redirect to registered callback (code, state)
        Browser -> AppA: GET /sso/callback?code=...&state=...
        AppA -> AppA: Validate state + transaction cookie
        AppA -> SSO: POST /sso/exchange (backend)\n{ code, codeVerifier, redirectUri }
        SSO -> SSO: Check current session + grant;\nvalidate proof and atomically consume code
        SSO --> AppA: { accessToken } for application A
        AppA --> Browser: Set own verified JWT cookie;\nredirect to saved returnUrl
    end
end

== Enter Application B ==

Browser -> AppB: Open protected URL / registered start
ref over Browser, AppB
    Repeat state/PKCE authorization for B.
    A valid central identity with B access needs no new email.
    B exchanges its own code and stores its own JWT cookie.
end ref

note over Browser, AppB
Optional /sso/apps launcher lists applications from current grants.
Its Open links use registered app start routes; launcher sign-in
creates central identity only. Each app session remains independent.
end note

== Local and Central Sign-Out ==

opt Sign out of application A
    Browser -> AppA: POST local logout (same-origin)
    AppA --> Browser: Clear/revoke local session; public signed-out page
end
opt End browser SSO session
    Browser -> SSO: GET /sso/signout (confirmation only)
    Browser -> SSO: Confirm; POST /sso/signout (CSRF)
    SSO -> SSO: Revoke central session and pending codes
    SSO --> Browser: Clear central cookie; signed-out destination
end

note over Browser, AppB
Local logout retains central identity. Central logout prevents new
automatic sign-ins; existing app JWTs keep their expiry/revocation policy.
Gate uses namespaced routes; Django uses trailing slashes.
All issuer browser visits are top-level document navigations.
end note

@enduml
